    "content": "The four astronauts selected for NASA's Artemis II mission, set to fly around the moon in 2026, are Commander Reid Wiseman, Pilot Victor Glover, Mission Specialist 1 Christina Koch, and Mission Specialist 2 Jeremy Hansen. This crew represents the first lunar mission in over 50 years and includes the first woman, person of color, and non-U.S. citizen to venture beyond low Earth orbit. Artemis II Crew Details: Reid Wiseman (NASA Commander): A former Navy test pilot and flight engineer who previously served on the International Space Station. Victor Glover (NASA Pilot): A U.S. Navy commander who was the pilot on the Crew-1 SpaceX Crew Dragon. He will be the first African American to travel to the moon. Christina Koch (NASA Mission Specialist): An electrical engineer who holds the record for the longest single spaceflight by a woman (328 days) and was part of the first all-female spacewalk. Jeremy Hansen (CSA Mission Specialist): A Canadian Space Agency astronaut, he is the first Canadian to travel to the moon. Mission Overview: Goal: To test the Orion capsule's life support systems with humans on board, paving the way for future lunar landings. Duration: Approximately 10 days, with the astronauts expected to venture further from Earth than any human in history. Not Landing: The mission will orbit the moon but will not land; the landing is scheduled for the subsequent Artemis III mission. You can read more detailed profiles of the crew from sources like the BBC and The New York Times. the BBC The New York Times",
